From 1f739abe041828768831c67952b497aadd778b44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stringer <jcec_1@yahoo.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:40:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] render: the changed-line hook names the surface row in
 scanline mode

With ScanLines set (RENDERING_ACCURACY_HIGH, a host's hires picture) CPC line i
is copied to surface row Render_ScreenYOffset + 2i, with the rows between left
black, but Render_LineChangedHook was called with Render_ScreenYOffset + i, so
a host converting only the changed rows redrew the wrong ones and kept stale
lines on screen (BASIC MODE 2 scrolling: 33000 of 36000 changed rows missed).
The hook now gets the row the line was written to. Without ScanLines (the
normal picture) nothing changes, and the pixels drawn are the same either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/cpc/render5.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cpc/render5.c b/src/cpc/render5.c
index e01a419..c88a30a 100644
--- a/src/cpc/render5.c
+++ b/src/cpc/render5.c
@@ -1608,7 +1608,10 @@ void    Render_DumpScreen4(void)
 							if (k < n)
 							{
 								for (; k < n; k++) d[k] = s[k];
-								Render_LineChangedHook(Render_ScreenYOffset + i);
+								/* hires (ScanLines): the surface pitch was doubled above, so CPC line i is
+								 * surface row 2i (every other row is left black), not row i; marking row i
+								 * left the changed rows stale on the AGA screen (1.2 fix; lores: i, as before) */
+								Render_LineChangedHook(Render_ScreenYOffset + (ScanLines ? (i << 1) : i));
 							}
 						}
 						else
